From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Caboose <caboose@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] Offer the device features Direct3D 11 needs that the host GPU
 lacks

DXVK refuses a device without geometryShader, shaderCullDistance,
VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable and VK_EXT_robustness2 nullDescriptor and
robustBufferAccess2, and Zink refuses one without nullDescriptor; Metal,
under the phone's MoltenVK, has none of them. When the host lacks one the
driver offers it and keeps it from the host
(caboose-features/d3d11_emulation.h, d3d11_tracker.inc):

- null descriptors, vertex buffers and index buffers become zeroed
  stand-ins the driver makes per device; VK_EXT_robustness2 itself is
  offered when the host lacks the extension;
- a pipeline with a geometry stage keeps its vertex stage alone and
  discards rasterization: its draws produce nothing;
- cull distance variables become private, in vkCreateShaderModule and in
  a stage's own shader module;
- a depth clip state becomes the pipeline's depth clamp.

The host's features are learned from the feature query, or asked once at
device creation, which now keeps every offered feature (0035's logicOp
too) from the host. VK_KHR_maintenance5, VK_KHR_maintenance6 and
VK_KHR_load_store_op_none, which DXVK also requires, pass through, and a
bind's VkBindMemoryStatus reports the call's result.
